# Weekly CLAIMS UPDATE to the recipient list Finance keep.
#
# WHY (B1, requested by Bokani Makosha): Finance rebuilt this every week out of
# the Graphite "Claims As On Date (Inception-to-Date)" export — paste, derive the
# group from the policy number, pivot by month reported, total the reserve and
# payment columns, email it. The export and the email are mechanical.
#
# 05:00 UTC MONDAY = 07:00 Monday in Gaborone (Botswana never observes DST, so
# this offset is fixed year-round) — the CFO's decision, so the position is on
# Finance's desk when they start the week. Day-of-week 1 is Monday.
#
# NOT a date-of-loss report. The month is the month the claim was REPORTED.
#
# omni-manage, NOT `docker compose exec`: the raw form was retired on 2026-09-04
# after a cron ran mid blue/green flip and the company lost a day's attendance
# record. The wrapper waits for a healthy container instead of writing into a
# dying one.
#
# Read-only. It SELECTs from the Graphite claims mirror and sends an email. It
# raises no payment, changes no claim and moves no money. It exits NON-ZERO when
# the mirror is unreadable, when no claim has ever had its detail synced (every
# money figure would be zero and it would read as a quiet month), or when the
# recipient list is empty — so a broken Monday never looks like a calm one.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

0 5 * * 1 root /usr/local/bin/omni-manage send_weekly_claims_report >> /var/log/alpha-finance/weekly-claims-update.log 2>&1
